<script setup>
const props=defineProps({report:Object,settings:{type:Object,required:true}}),emit=defineEmits(['change']);
const set=(key,value)=>emit('change',{...props.settings,[key]:value});
</script>
<template><section aria-label="Furniture clearance settings"><h3>Furniture clearance</h3><label>Minimum furniture wall gap metres<input :value="settings.minWall" type="number" min="0" max="2" step="0.01" @input="set('minWall',$event.target.value===''?NaN:Number($event.target.value))"></label><label>Door access depth metres<input :value="settings.doorDepth" type="number" min="0" max="3" step="0.05" @input="set('doorDepth',$event.target.value===''?NaN:Number($event.target.value))"></label><label class="snap-toggle"><input :checked="settings.enforce" type="checkbox" aria-label="Enforce clearance for preview insertion" @change="set('enforce',$event.target.checked)">Enforce clearance for preview insertion</label><p v-if="report?.error" role="status">{{ report.error }}</p><template v-else-if="report"><p data-testid="selected-wall-clearance">Nearest wall {{ report.nearestWall.wall }} · {{ report.nearestWall.distance.toFixed(3) }} m</p><ul v-if="report.issues.length" data-testid="selected-clearance-issues"><li v-for="(issue,n) in report.issues" :key="n">{{ issue.message }}</li></ul><p v-else class="hint">No issues under these planning settings.</p></template><p class="hint">Workspace planning settings, not building-code checks. Inward doors use a conservative rectangle as deep as the door width or access depth; outward doors use access depth. Windows use a 0.15 m service zone when cabinet height extends above the sill. Enforcement affects preview confirmations only; direct edits remain advisory. Handles and true door-sweep geometry are excluded.</p></section></template>
